## ⚙️ JavaScript Standards

### Rules

- ES6+ always: `const`/`let`, arrow functions, `async/await`, template literals, destructuring
- No jQuery, no lodash, no external JS beyond GSAP + ScrollReveal (on CDN)
- All API calls use native `fetch()`
- Every async function wrapped in `try/catch`
- No `alert()` / `confirm()` / `prompt()` — ever. Use styled UI elements.
- Loading states for every async operation
- Debounce scroll/resize handlers

### Error Display Pattern

```javascript
function showError(containerEl, message) {
  containerEl.innerHTML = `
    <div class="alert alert-error" role="alert">
      <svg class="alert-icon" ...></svg>
      <div class="alert-content">
        <strong>Error</strong>
        <p>${message}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  `;
}
```

### Loading State Pattern

```javascript
function setLoading(buttonEl, containerEl, isLoading, message = 'Please wait...') {
  buttonEl.disabled = isLoading;
  buttonEl.textContent = isLoading ? message : buttonEl.dataset.defaultText;
  if (isLoading) {
    containerEl.innerHTML = `
      <div class="loading-wrap">
        <div class="loading-spinner"></div>
        <p class="loading-text">${message}</p>
      </div>
    `;
  }
}
```

### Admin Password Hashing

```javascript
async function hashPassword(password) {
  const encoder = new TextEncoder();
  const data = encoder.encode(password);
  const hash = await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', data);
  return Array.from(new Uint8Array(hash))
    .map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0'))
    .join('');
}
```

### Report ID Generator

```javascript
async function generateReportId() {
  const year = new Date().getFullYear();
  // Fetch existing count from Sheets
  const url = `https://sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets/${CONFIG.SHEETS_ID}/values/${CONFIG.SHEET_RANGE}?key=${CONFIG.GOOGLE_API_KEY}`;
  const res = await fetch(url);
  const data = await res.json();
  const count = (data.values?.length || 1) - 1; // subtract header row
  return `DDSE-${year}-${String(count + 1).padStart(3, '0')}`;
}
```

---

## 🔒 Security Notes

The admin panel uses **client-side password protection** (SHA-256 hash comparison). This is appropriate for this project because:
- No personal user data is stored server-side
- The static site has no server-side auth capability
- The worst-case breach is unauthorized report upload (not data theft)
- Google Drive/Sheets access can be revoked instantly by revoking the OAuth token
- For additional security, the admin page URL can be non-obvious (e.g., `/mgmt-panel.html`)

Staff sessions stored in `sessionStorage` — cleared when tab closes.

