## ✅ HTML/CSS Code Quality Rules

1. Every HTML file: full `<head>` with charset, viewport, title, meta description, OG tags, favicon, preconnect, CSS links
2. Every page: identical navbar and footer markup (copy-paste consistent)
3. **No inline styles** — all styles in CSS files only
4. **No inline JavaScript** — all JS in `<script src>` at bottom of `<body>`
5. **Semantic HTML**: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>`, `<aside>` used correctly
6. All images: `alt` attribute always set (descriptive, not "image")
7. CSS: variables from `:root` only — **zero hardcoded color hex values in CSS**
8. Forms: every `<input>` has a `<label>` linked by `for`/`id`
9. External links: always `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`
10. Accessibility: all interactive elements keyboard-navigable; focus states styled; ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
11. Animations: always check `prefers-reduced-motion` before GSAP plays
12. `will-change: transform` on elements animated by GSAP

